  "reputation": {
    "summary": "An OEM and engineering favourite rather than a rolling legend, since it is SMD only. Low noise and distortion at modest current. Reported design wins (Soomal, Frieve reviews; maker pages): iBasso DX90 DAC I/V (with OPA1611 and BUF634) and Cayin RU3 dongle (with SGM8262). No op-amp-specific listening tests or ASR measurements found.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [
      "neutral (DX90 as whole)",
      "restrained, relaxed",
      "slightly soft mids"
    ],
    "typical_uses": [
      "DAC I/V conversion (iBasso DX90, per Soomal)",
      "Parallel-drive dongle output stage (Cayin RU3)",
      "LME49720/LM4562 replacement in new designs (reportedly TI-suggested)",
      "Transformerless balanced line driver (DIY XPS project)",
      "Multichannel mixers and filter banks (OPA1604)"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "SMD only (SOIC/MSOP/TSSOP); a DIP-8 socket needs an adapter board.",
      "About ±30 mA drive suits line level; headphone designs add BUF634s or parallel sections.",
      "1.8 pA/√Hz current noise raises noise with high source impedances.",
      "Absolute max allows a short to VS/2 for only one amplifier per package.",
      "No op-amp-specific stability or oscillation reports found."
    ],
    "sources": [
